# iOS components

The SwiftUI building block for each component in [../../components.md](../../components.md), where iOS differs. Mobile
behaviour: [../components.md](../components.md). Conventions: [ios.md](ios.md).

| Component | SwiftUI |
|---|---|
| Button | `Button` with a project `ButtonStyle` built from the theme; height at least 44pt. |
| Input | `TextField` / `SecureField` with a label above; `.keyboardType` and `.submitLabel` set. |
| Select | `Picker` (menu or wheel) or `Menu`; long lists use a pushed list. |
| Checkbox, radio, switch | `Toggle` (switch); checkbox and radio are `Toggle` or a `Picker` with a custom style. |
| Card | A `VStack` on the theme's surface colour and radius. |
| Badge, chip | A small `Label` view: icon plus word. |
| Dialog | `.alert` or `.confirmationDialog`. |
| Sheet | `.sheet` with detents only when needed. |
| Menu | `Menu` or `.contextMenu`. |
| Tabs | `TabView` (top-level) or a `Picker` with `.segmented`. |
| Toast | A small overlay view, announced with an accessibility notification. |
| Empty / error state | `ContentUnavailableView` styled with the theme. |
| Skeleton | `.redacted(reason: .placeholder)`. |

Add the project's own SwiftUI components here, with the file they live in; update [../../inventory.md](../../inventory.md).
